WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.320
Cunning, liar, enigmatic, and fearsome&nbsp;
are just a few words used to describe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:11.840
a particular member of the SCP Foundation.&nbsp;
While many of the Foundation’s researchers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:17.920
scientists are a pretty unusual bunch, to say&nbsp;
the least, this one might just take the cake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.440
and then might have said cake “decommissioned”&nbsp;
in the most collaterally damaging way imaginable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.080
Similar to the infamous Doctor Bright always&nbsp;
switching bodies, appearing with all manner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:34.320
of ever-shifting faces, genders, and even species,&nbsp;
this particular Foundation department head is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.560
no stranger to never looking the same way twice.
In his case, he can’t be photographed properly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:46.480
at least not by any conventional means.&nbsp;
Thanks to some unknown anomalous augmentation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.520
any pictures taken of this researcher will have&nbsp;
the face swapped with that of a random animal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.240
However, these pictures will always feature the&nbsp;
same characteristic grin much like the smile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:03.280
of the Cheshire Cat. A notorious liar not to be&nbsp;
trusted by anyone, Doctor Alto Clef is one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:09.440
SCP Foundation’s strangest members of personnel.
For starters, “Doctor Alto Clef” isn’t even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:15.520
technically his real name, more a nickname that&nbsp;
became synonymous with the mysterious scientist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.640
and served as a convenient shorthand&nbsp;
for his alleged real name. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.920
according to the entity most commonly known as&nbsp;
Doctor Clef, his real name is actually a sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:33.200
unpronounceable by human beings. His name is,&nbsp;
apparently, the A major chord played on a ukulele.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.360
This explains why the strange doctor always&nbsp;
carries the instrument around with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:42.320
should anyone wish to refer to him using&nbsp;
his real name on a strum of those strings.&nbsp;

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:48.080
In fact, he used to go by a completely different&nbsp;
name, the “Ukulele Man”, and sometimes “Agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:54.320
Ukulele”, thanks to his predilection for playing&nbsp;
the string instrument. So, where did the “Alto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:00.240
Clef” nickname come from? Well, that one’s easy,&nbsp;
Doctor Clef received this nickname thanks to his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:06.160
penchant for signing off reports with a hand-drawn&nbsp;
alto clef symbol, a type of musical note.&nbsp;

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.960
Doctor Clef had long been one of the more&nbsp;
enigmatic and mysterious scientists working at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:17.920
Foundation. He is perhaps more of an oddity than&nbsp;
the elusive and infamous O5 Council themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.640
although that one is probably up for debate.&nbsp;
Alto Clef was formerly an operative for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.680
Global Occult Coalition, although he first&nbsp;
attracted the attention of the SCP Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:32.960
a while before then. A number of research papers&nbsp;
Clef published at a redacted university happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.920
to catch the Foundation’s eye, mostly for&nbsp;
their bizarre and lurid subject matter.&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.600
Much of the content and even the title of some&nbsp;
of his works are redacted, but what we do know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.720
is that one of Clef’s papers described certain&nbsp;
traits that matched an existing SCP they had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:55.120
cataloged in their archive. There was no way this&nbsp;
could have been a coincidence, somehow Alto Clef&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:00.720
had knowledge of the anomalous, and had to&nbsp;
be considered a potential risk to security.&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.600
During a conversation with the agent that was&nbsp;
sent to investigate his strange research papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.760
Alto Clef was able to convince her to&nbsp;
offer him a job within the Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:15.200
It seems exceptionally unusual that Clef was&nbsp;
able to pull this off, as most women working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:21.520
for the SCP Foundation have reported that the&nbsp;
man possesses a positively slimy personality.&nbsp;

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:27.520
So, why even bother to hire this guy if he seems&nbsp;
to be such a creep? Well, it turned out that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:33.200
acquisition of Doctor Clef wasn’t without its&nbsp;
advantages, namely the capture and containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:40.880
of SCP-447. This SCP, for any who might be&nbsp;
unfamiliar, is an anomaly in two parts. The first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:47.840
SCP-447-1, is a sphere composed entirely of a&nbsp;
green, slime-like substance. It’s warm to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:53.920
touch, the same sort of heat as an ordinary human&nbsp;
body, and has no adverse or harmful effects on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:04:01.040
anyone that comes into contact with it. SCP-447-2&nbsp;
is a viscous green slime that is excreted by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:06.720
main ball. This excretion can be eaten, or can&nbsp;
increase the fuel efficiency of gasoline by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:12.160
one hundred and fifty percent when they are mixed.
The sphere and the substance are only known to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.840
harmful when they come into contact with dead&nbsp;
bodies, although what exactly occurs when this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:23.680
happens has been redacted by the O5 Council.
Nonetheless, Doctor Alto Clef was reportedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:29.840
instrumental in retrieving SCP-447, and given&nbsp;
the usefulness of its slime to the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:36.000
the doctor had, in turn, proved his own worth. The&nbsp;
consensus seems to be that, while his personality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:42.480
might be annoying or even outright repulsive in&nbsp;
some instances, Alto Clef is still able to perform&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:49.040
his job with precision and competence, making&nbsp;
the doctor a useful asset to the SCP Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.320
During his time there, Clef became well known&nbsp;
for being somewhat of a gun enthusiast as well.&nbsp;

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.720
In fact, he earned his own brand of infamy&nbsp;
for his habit of brutally “decommissioning”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:04.960
dangerous SCPs; and you can probably guess what&nbsp;
we mean by that. In other words, Clef established&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:11.520
himself as the Foundation’s go-to executioner.
Sometimes, he’s a little too good at his job&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.560
though. In one instance, Clef brought a chainsaw&nbsp;
to work that he thought possessed supernatural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.520
properties. However, this happened to take place&nbsp;
at the Foundation’s annual costume party, causing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:27.440
the doctor to think that a riot was taking place,&nbsp;
thanks to personnel all being dressed as D Class.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.240
Chainsaw in hand, Clef murdered half of his&nbsp;
own research staff without a second thought.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:37.360
It also turned out that the chainsaw hadn’t had&nbsp;
any anomalous properties in the first place.&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:44.320
Doctor Clef is renowned for having brutal&nbsp;
efficiency, not shying away from causing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.720
the deaths of countless civilian lives&nbsp;
during his “decommissioning” of anomalies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:54.240
As long as he is able to kill or contain an SCP&nbsp;
to further the course of science, or protect the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:59.200
majority of the civilian world, then Clef will&nbsp;
view any possible deaths and collateral damage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:06.640
caused by his actions as acceptable losses.&nbsp;
In short, he is a necessary evil. But perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:12.400
Clef’s best-known attempt at decommissioning&nbsp;
an anomaly was during the SCP-239 Incident.&nbsp;

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:17.920
Also known by the nickname of “The Witch&nbsp;
Child”, SCP-239 might appear to be a harmless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:22.880
eight-year-old child, but she’s actually a&nbsp;
powerful reality-bending anomaly, with impervious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:29.120
indestructible skin. Her capabilities are almost&nbsp;
limitless, and she can influence the world and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:35.200
people around her in virtually any way that she&nbsp;
can imagine. As long as she is conscious and can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:42.880
see her surroundings, SCP-239 can create living&nbsp;
matter, or make it disappear, wishing things into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:49.040
or out of existence with as little as a simple&nbsp;
thought. Or, as her file in the SCP Archive puts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:54.880
it, “If she can see it, she can change it.”
Although SCP-239 was being contained by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.880 --> 00:07:00.000
Foundation, given a pre-approved list of “spells”&nbsp;
that she was allowed to perform and kept calm at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.680
all times so she wouldn’t think to cause harm to&nbsp;
herself or anyone around her, Doctor Clef didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:10.880
think this was adequate enough. In a report, he&nbsp;
claimed that the Witch Child’s containment wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:16.880
suitable and that she posed a major security risk&nbsp;
to the SCP Foundation and its personnel. You see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.760
given his time with the Global Occult Coalition,&nbsp;
Doctor Clef had become somewhat of an expert in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:28.560
anomalies with the ability to reshape reality,&nbsp;
making him particularly wary of SCP-239.&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.480
It was his proposal that the Foundation&nbsp;
should not overestimate its own ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:37.200
to contain these reality benders, and&nbsp;
that they should instead strike first.&nbsp;

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:44.080
Doctor Clef’s idea was simple: Use some form&nbsp;
of sharp implement to kill SCP-239. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:49.520
given the Witch Child’s impenetrable skin, this&nbsp;
is a lot easier said than done. But Clef had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:54.480
few solutions handy to work around this. Firstly,&nbsp;
his plan was that this decommissioning would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:08:00.000
carried out at night when SCP-239 was asleep,&nbsp;
and as a result, her reality-altering powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.600
would be neutralized. Second, the implement&nbsp;
used to kill her would be made out of SCP-148,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:10.880
the “Telekill” Alloy. This anomaly is a metal&nbsp;
that the Foundation keeps stored in blocks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.840
that has the unique property of being able&nbsp;
to block telepathic and memetic effects.&nbsp;

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:20.240
Now, that plan on its own might sound fine&nbsp;
on paper - that is, if you’re on board with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:26.080
murdering an eight-year-old SCP while she’s&nbsp;
asleep - But there were a number of risks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:32.320
for Clef to consider. SCP-239 could wake up during&nbsp;
her termination, and would then be able to resist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:38.480
being killed. But another far more complicated&nbsp;
risk was that SCP-239 could wake up, perceive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:43.360
the person carrying out her termination as a&nbsp;
friend, as someone who wouldn’t harm her, and her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:48.960
abilities would then alter the world around her&nbsp;
to make this the case, changing reality to match.&nbsp;

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.440
To try and avoid this outcome, Doctor Clef&nbsp;
volunteered himself as the one who would carry out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:59.120
the procedure. With his mysterious past, dealing&nbsp;
with reality-changing anomalies as a member of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:05.520
Global Occult Coalition, he overzealously thought&nbsp;
he was the only man cut out for the job. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.800
in his arrogance, Clef made the fatal mistake&nbsp;
of transmitting his plan openly to Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:17.920
personnel, instead of using secure, encrypted&nbsp;
channels. You see, over time, SCP-239 had formed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.880
bonds with a number of the Site 17 staff that&nbsp;
had been assigned to her. Regardless of whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:27.280
staff members had sympathy towards the girl,&nbsp;
or because her perception of them had altered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:33.840
reality and bent their intentions, Dr. Kondraki&nbsp;
had to step in and intervene. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:38.800
this led to an altercation between the two.
Thanks to Kondraki’s efforts, Doctor Clef’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:45.520
proposed plan of decommissioning SCP-239, a&nbsp;
defenseless, anomalous child, was thwarted.&nbsp;

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:49.280
Even so, during the incident,&nbsp;
Clef showed how remarkably,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:54.800
and worryingly, easy he found it to outwit&nbsp;
the Foundation’s defenses and security forces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.800 --> 00:10:00.640
Though he walked away from his attempted murder&nbsp;
of SCP-239 with a few severe injuries, Clef’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:06.720
career wasn’t impeded upon in the slightest. In&nbsp;
fact, the O5 Council promoted him to the position&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:11.520
of Department Head for the SCP Foundation’s&nbsp;
Division of Training and Development, thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:17.600
to his reputation for swift, relentless, and&nbsp;
surgically precise methods of terminating SCPs.&nbsp;

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:23.200
However, Doctor Clef’s actions during the SCP-239&nbsp;
Incident prompted some within the Foundation to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:28.880
take a closer look at his past. A tricky thing&nbsp;
to do, especially seeing as Clef is known to be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:34.000
liar and not someone to be trusted, and that this&nbsp;
has been a long-time habit of his that is unlikely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:39.040
to change. However, there does exist a service&nbsp;
record for a Global Occult Coalition operative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:45.200
who used to go by the code name of ‘Ukulele’.
First recruited into the Coalition in 1981,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.560
Ukulele was reported to have killed a&nbsp;
number of Known Threat Entities (or KTEs),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:54.960
but these usually came with the result of&nbsp;
heavy casualties, including the deaths of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.960 --> 00:11:00.800
other GOC operatives. One Colonel Richard Adams&nbsp;
is quoted in Ukulele’s service record as saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.880
“Does anyone know who this guy is or where&nbsp;
he came from? He's good at what he does,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:08.880
right, but every time I ask him about his&nbsp;
past, I get a completely different answer.”&nbsp;

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:14.320
Eventually, after ninety-nine confirmed kills of&nbsp;
anomalous entities, the operative known as Ukulele&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:19.680
expressed a desire to retire from active service&nbsp;
within the Coalition. This request was granted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:26.800
and sometime later, he resurfaced working for the&nbsp;
SCP Foundation under a new name: Doctor Alto Clef.&nbsp;

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:32.080
Naturally, Doctor Clef has never confirmed nor&nbsp;
denied that he is, in fact, Ukulele, although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:37.040
his habit of playing the instrument does seem to&nbsp;
imply that there’s some sort of connection there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:42.160
After all, that’s not as strange as some of the&nbsp;
other rumors floating around about our old friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:47.840
Alto Clef. Some think he’s an incarnation of&nbsp;
the Devil himself, or that he even married&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:52.800
a goddess and had several children with her.
Others claim Clef is the biological father of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.800 --> 00:12:00.320
SCP-166, a girl with deer horns and the ability to&nbsp;
make anything man-made corrode. Then again, you’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:05.440
be better off coming up with your own answer than&nbsp;
asking Doctor Clef about his past. He’s hardly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:11.360
likely to give you a straight answer, providing&nbsp;
he doesn’t ‘accidentally’ kill you on the spot.&nbsp;

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:17.120
Now go check out “SCP Foundation Boss - The&nbsp;
Administrator Explained” and “SCP Immortal Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:23.600
Bright Explained” for more of the inside scoop on&nbsp;
the mysterious figures behind the SCP Foundation!

